---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy & Local Data | Online Stopwatch"
  description="Understand how Online Stopwatch stores your session and preferences locally in your browser, and how to delete them."
>
  <main id="main" class="wrap prose-page">
    <span class="eyebrow">YOUR TIME STAYS YOURS</span>
    <h1>Privacy & local data.</h1>
    <p>Last updated: October 10, 2026</p>
    <p>
      This page explains the data behavior of Online Stopwatch, a Wearlivo tool,
      and its timer features.
    </p>
    <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The tools use browser local storage to save stopwatch sessions, lap
      records, countdown deadlines, routines, sound preferences, and custom
      display choices. The application does not send this session data to a
      server.
    </p>
    <h2>No account required</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not require an account. Fonts are served with the
      website, and the stopwatch application does not set its own tracking
      cookies.
    </p>
    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics to understand aggregate website use, such as the
      pages people visit and how they arrive at the site. Google may process
      browser, device, and usage information according to its own privacy
      practices. This analytics service does not receive your stopwatch laps,
      saved routines, or local timer sessions because those records stay in your
      browser.
    </p>
    <h2>Control your session</h2>
    <p>
      Open Settings on any stopwatch and choose “Clear local data” to remove all
      saved tool sessions and preferences. Resetting the stopwatch removes the
      current session. Your browser’s site-data controls can also remove all
      local storage. Private browsing or storage restrictions may prevent
      recovery.
    </p>
    <h2>Custom setup links</h2>
    <p>
      Copying a custom stopwatch setup link includes your session title and
      appearance choices in the URL. Anyone with that link can read those
      settings. Lap records and timer history are not included. Avoid putting
      private information in a title you plan to share. The URL may also appear
      in browser history and website request logs.
    </p>
    <h2>Exports and shared devices</h2>
    <p>
      CSV downloads and copied results are created only when you request them.
      Downloaded files remain wherever you save them; clearing browser data does
      not remove those files. Someone using the same browser profile may be able
      to restore your session, so clear local data after using a shared device.
    </p>
    <h2>Website requests</h2>
    <p>
      Loading the website requires ordinary network requests. The hosting
      provider may process connection details such as your IP address and
      requested URLs to serve the website. This application does not control the
      hosting provider’s infrastructure logs.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions about privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Contact <a href="mailto:hello@wearlivo.com">hello@wearlivo.com</a> with
      “Privacy” in the subject line, or visit <a href="/contact/">Contact Us</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/">Back to your stopwatch →</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
